			"date": "2024-12-05T02:51:57.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@rauschma\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>rauschma</span></a></span> I still have PTSD from cleaning up the mistakes of jQuery Deferred (and Dojo and Backbone relatives). I know this new API isn’t doomed to repeat the mistakes of the past and the same sorts of wild callback leaks just because it looks the same as some of the bad old predecessors Promises intentionally replaced, but I still worry what some devs are going to misuse with this all the same.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
